      "content": "It's definitely a good idea to keep an eye on it, but if the spots are just a heat rash, they should fade away on their own. Try giving him a cool bath with some calamine lotion to soothe the skin. If the fever persists or the spots worsen, you might want to consider a mild fever reducer like acetaminophen, but only if you're sure it's not something more serious. Just keep him hydrated and comfortable, and if you have any doubts, a quick call to your local clinic won't hurt.",
